-- examples/checks/ds-tree-holds-prov-check.rofl — ds_tree_holds, which keeps its witnesses: the closure of the tree is
-- derived as any rows are, so each of the two rules it lowers to has made a row of it (`derived_by`). A closure answered from
-- its tree where witnesses are kept would have no row to cite and no firing to say.
dstp_unmade(R) :- concludes(R, dst_within), not derived_by[$kernel](_, R, _).
alarm(dstp_unmade).
